[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: pc15
diagnosis_text:
The affected component is PC15’s host routing configuration (default gateway). PC15 is on VLAN 51 and can reach local peers, but any off-subnet traffic must go via its default gateway. On PC15 the route table shows default via 172.18.51.250, and its ARP/neighbor table shows 172.18.51.250 dev eth0 FAILED. Pings to that address return “Destination Host Unreachable” from 172.18.51.15 itself, indicating it cannot resolve or reach its configured next hop. In contrast, the actual gateway in this VLAN is reachable at 172.18.51.254 (PC15 can ping 172.18.51.254 successfully), and a peer (PC16) has default via 172.18.51.254 and can reach Laptop4 (172.18.50.14) without issue.

Mechanism: Because the default gateway on PC15 points to a nonexistent or wrong IP (172.18.51.250), ARP for that next hop fails and PC15 cannot forward packets to the 172.18.50.0/24 wireless network. Local subnet traffic (e.g., to 172.18.51.16) remains unaffected, explaining why PC15 can still ping neighbors.

Localization: PC15’s routing table and ARP cache on interface eth0.

Root cause: PC15’s default gateway is misconfigured to 172.18.51.250 instead of the correct 172.18.51.254.

Corrective fix: Reconfigure PC15’s default route to 172.18.51.254 and remove the bad route. For example:
- ip route del default via 172.18.51.250
- ip route add default via 172.18.51.254
Then persist via the host’s network config (e.g., /etc/network/interfaces or netplan) and optionally flush ARP (ip neigh flush all). After this, PC15 should reach 172.18.50.x. 
=== END ===